From 413df551e2be9c8dacd8b53ad05c0a7ea8efb9a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briheet-invideo <dev@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:41:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] arm64: idle: Preserve registers across WFI on M4 and
 later Apple cores

M4-generation cores (T8132, T6040, T6041) come back from WFI with their
general-purpose and FP/SIMD registers cleared; SP and memory survive.
iBoot locks CYC_OVRD, which on M1 to M3 keeps WFI retentive, so the boot
loaders pass idle=nop and every idle core spins.

Enter WFI through apple_cpu_wfi(), which keeps x18-x30 on the stack (the
call already clobbers x0-x17), after saving and dropping this CPU's
FP/SIMD state. Decide from smp_prepare_boot_cpu(), before the boot CPU
first idles.

Taken from aurora-silicon/linux integration/aurora: c407e1097ba7 (Ryan
Murray), 3f0822d73dbe (Diljit Singh), 34649b455f4a (Jonathan Goyvaerts),
without the T8142/T6050 idle=nop override and the WFxT override; this
kernel keeps arm64.nowfxt.

Co-developed-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-developed-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Co-developed-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
---
